usage: longbench_eval.py [-h] --model MODEL [--tasks TASKS [TASKS ...]]
                         [--methods METHODS [METHODS ...]] [--budget BUDGET]
                         [--max-samples MAX_SAMPLES] [--device DEVICE]
                         [--prefill-last-logits] [--data-dir DATA_DIR]
                         [--max-ctx MAX_CTX]
                         [--tiered-kv-dtype {float32,bfloat16,float16}]
                         [--tiered-stt-kv-dtype {same,float8_e4m3fn}]
                         [--tiered-prefill-chunk-size TIERED_PREFILL_CHUNK_SIZE]
                         [--seed SEED]
                         [--sttram-bifurcation-frac STTRAM_BIFURCATION_FRAC]
                         [--stt-live-floor STT_LIVE_FLOOR]
                         [--write-aware-lambda WRITE_AWARE_LAMBDA]
                         [--no-tiered-inclusive] [--json JSON]
                         [--checkpoint CHECKPOINT]
                         [--allow-checkpoint-mismatch]
                         [--tiered-vram-budget TIERED_VRAM_BUDGET]
                         [--tiered-stt-budget TIERED_STT_BUDGET]
                         [--recent-size RECENT_SIZE]
                         [--tiered-stt-expose TIERED_STT_EXPOSE]
                         [--tiered-promotion-budget TIERED_PROMOTION_BUDGET]

Run LongBench evaluation with fixed TieredKV implementation

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --model MODEL         HF model id or local path
  --tasks TASKS [TASKS ...]
  --methods METHODS [METHODS ...]
  --budget BUDGET       Total KV budget in tokens for eviction methods
  --max-samples MAX_SAMPLES
                        Limit samples per task for quick runs
  --device DEVICE
  --prefill-last-logits
                        Compute only the last prefill logits; requires native
                        logits_to_keep support
  --data-dir DATA_DIR   Local LongBench JSONL directory (preferred for
                        reproducibility)
  --max-ctx MAX_CTX     Prompt truncation length (middle-split), shared by
                        every method. Default 31500 matches the reference
                        LongBench protocol for mistral-7B-instruct-v0.2.
                        Lowering this shrinks the compression ratio and is NOT
                        comparable to published LongBench numbers -- report
                        the value you used.
  --tiered-kv-dtype {float32,bfloat16,float16}
                        Dtype TieredKV stores its K/V tiers in. Default
                        float32 reproduces every result measured so far, but
                        doubles the real footprint versus the bfloat16
                        baselines it is compared against. Use bfloat16 for a
                        footprint-honest equal-VRAM run. Eviction scores stay
                        float32 either way.
  --tiered-stt-kv-dtype {same,float8_e4m3fn}
                        Experimental cold-tier storage dtype. 'same' uses
                        --tiered-kv-dtype; float8_e4m3fn stores one byte per
                        element and converts selected rows before attention.
  --tiered-prefill-chunk-size TIERED_PREFILL_CHUNK_SIZE
                        Experimental TieredKV-only bounded prefill chunk size.
                        0 keeps exact full-prompt prefill; positive values
                        compress the cache after every chunk.
  --seed SEED           Seed for torch/numpy, recorded in the results config
                        so a run is identifiable.
  --sttram-bifurcation-frac STTRAM_BIFURCATION_FRAC
                        Fraction of TieredKV's STT-RAM budget that bifurcation
                        may fill with cold prompt tokens; the rest is reserved
                        headroom for decode-time victim-cache backups. 1.0 =
                        original behavior (STT-RAM starts full, write savings
                        measure ~0% on long documents). Lower values trade
                        prompt-token recall for genuine write savings -- see
                        TieredConfig.sttram_bifurcation_frac in
                        src/tiered_kv_cache.py.
  --stt-live-floor STT_LIVE_FLOOR
                        Minimum live (non-shadow) STT rows promote() leaves
                        per layer. Prevents one fully-shadowed layer from
                        vetoing slow-tier exposure for all layers (measured
                        starvation on hotpotqa). See
                        TieredConfig.stt_live_floor.
  --write-aware-lambda WRITE_AWARE_LAMBDA
                        Write-aware demotion weight: victim score =
                        avg_attention - lambda * has_backup, preferring zero-
                        write re-demotions among near-tied cold tokens. 0.0 =
                        pure recall eviction. See
                        TieredConfig.write_aware_lambda.
  --no-tiered-inclusive
                        Paired no-shadow ablation: remove the slow-tier copy
                        on promotion, so re-demotion pays a write. All other
                        budgets and policy settings stay fixed.
  --json JSON
  --checkpoint CHECKPOINT
                        checkpoint file to resume from
  --allow-checkpoint-mismatch
                        Resume from a checkpoint even if its recorded config
                        (model/budget/tiered-vram/tiered-stt/stt-
                        expose/bifurcation-frac) doesn't match this run's
                        args. Without this flag, a mismatch raises instead of
                        silently blending scores from two different configs
                        into one results table.
  --tiered-vram-budget TIERED_VRAM_BUDGET
                        Override TieredKV's VRAM (fast-tier) budget directly,
                        instead of deriving it as --budget // 3. Use this
                        together with --tiered-stt-budget to run the equal-
                        VRAM comparison (same fast-tier bytes as a baseline's
                        full --budget, plus a slow tier on top) rather than
                        the equal-total-budget comparison.
  --tiered-stt-budget TIERED_STT_BUDGET
                        Override TieredKV's STT-RAM (slow-tier) budget
                        directly. See --tiered-vram-budget.
  --recent-size RECENT_SIZE
                        Sliding-window (recent-token) size, shared by all
                        sink/window-based methods. Default: max(16, budget //
                        8).
  --tiered-stt-expose TIERED_STT_EXPOSE
                        Cap on how many STT-RAM tokens TieredKV actually
                        attends to per decode step (independent of --tiered-
                        stt-budget, which is how many are physically
                        resident). Bounds TieredKV's final attention pool to
                        sram_budget + this value, so it can be matched exactly
                        against a baseline's --budget for a fair equal-
                        attention comparison. Default:
                        promote_top_pages*page_size (32).
  --tiered-promotion-budget TIERED_PROMOTION_BUDGET
                        Maximum slow-tier rows promoted into VRAM per layer
                        and policy step. Attention exposure remains controlled
                        independently by --tiered-stt-expose. Default 32
                        preserves the corrected control; 0 disables migration
                        while retaining slow attention.
